WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.997
We're raising our girls to be perfect,

00:00:02.997 --> 00:00:06.419
and&nbsp;we're raising our boys to be brave.

00:00:06.419 --> 00:00:09.302
Most girls are taught to avoid risk and failure.

00:00:09.302 --> 00:00:11.188
Their taught to smile pretty,

00:00:11.188 --> 00:00:12.483
play it safe,

00:00:12.483 --> 00:00:13.680
get all A's.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.903
Boys, on the other hand, are 
taught to&nbsp;play rough.

00:00:17.903 --> 00:00:19.662
And by the time they're adults,

00:00:19.662 --> 00:00:21.969
whether they're negotiating a raise or

00:00:21.969 --> 00:00:24.229
even&nbsp;asking someone out on a date,

00:00:24.229 --> 00:00:28.210
they're habituated to take risk after risk.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.656
They're rewarded&nbsp;for it.

00:00:29.656 --> 00:00:32.889
An HP report found that 
men will apply for a job

00:00:32.889 --> 00:00:36.828
if they meet only 60 percent&nbsp;
of the qualifications,

00:00:36.828 --> 00:00:38.334
but women,

00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:42.699
women will apply only if 
they meet 100 percent.

00:00:42.699 --> 00:00:45.936
The bravery&nbsp;deficit is why women 
are underrepresented in STEM,

00:00:45.936 --> 00:00:50.687
in C-suites, in boardrooms, in Congress, 
and&nbsp;pretty much everywhere you look.

00:00:50.687 --> 00:00:54.401
We have to socialize our girls to 
be comfortable with&nbsp;imperfection,

00:00:54.401 --> 00:00:57.849
and we've got to do it now.

